1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,782
This is the failure we want to see. A stale-schema candidate reaches
EvidenceBound and returns BLOCKED with SCHEMA MISMATCH. The runtime
result stays null, promotion authorization stays false, and no
deployment or transaction claim is made.

2
00:00:12,232 --> 00:00:24,553
EvidenceBound DataHub Gate adds a narrow boundary between metadata
access and human approval: Read Context, Restricted AST Gate, Tamper-
Evident Proof Pack, and Native DataHub Write-Back. Mandatory Human
Review remains outside automation.

3
00:00:25,003 --> 00:00:37,757
The accepted live run used the DataHub showcase order-history dataset.
MCP discovered this exact URN, read entity and schema context, obtained
lineage evidence, ran both candidate paths, and appended both receipts
to the same description.

4
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:50,085
The read is deliberately bounded to one lineage hop and five results.
Upstream is checked first; after a visible edge, the opposite direction
is skipped. This avoids unbounded expansion, while missing lineage still
blocks verification.

5
00:00:50,535 --> 00:01:04,679
The candidate enters the deterministic gate. Dataset identity and
observed digests bind first. The Restricted AST Policy rejects
unsupported constructs. Supported operations run in a Fail-Closed
Bounded Interpreter without exec, and claims require evidence
references.

6
00:01:05,129 --> 00:01:18,766
With current DataHub context, the candidate matches observed schema and
lineage digests, producing VERIFIED. The verdict covers only the
recorded candidate, context, policy, and interpreter. Promotion remains
false and human review remains required.

7
00:01:19,216 --> 00:01:29,936
Change only the expected schema digest. The source does not run.
EvidenceBound returns BLOCKED with SCHEMA MISMATCH, a different Proof
Pack root, and no runtime result. Stale contracts do not silently pass.

8
00:01:30,386 --> 00:01:44,692
Both outcomes become Native DataHub Description Receipts through
official update description. Each records verdict, Proof Pack root,
digests, reasons, human review, and false promotion authorization. It is
graph-visible metadata evidence, not a badge or production
authorization.

9
00:01:45,142 --> 00:02:00,435
Each result becomes a Tamper-Evident Content-Addressed Proof Pack. The
retained VERIFIED pack reproduced with manifest b41f; the BLOCKED pack
with 3f83. Candidate, context, receipt, MCP evidence, manifest, and
SHA-256 sums remain inspectable.

10
00:02:00,885 --> 00:02:12,989
Tamper evidence is executable. The public test appends one byte to gate-
receipt JSON and reruns verification. The required result is ARTIFACT
TAMPERING DETECTED. This is hash-based detection, not a digital-
signature claim.

11
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:30,560
The implementation is public at moneyparking slash evidencebound datahub
gate. Accepted commit c8279f is validated by Actions run 30833135318.
Checkout, Python setup, installation, and deterministic validation all
succeeded.

12
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:45,604
The architecture is deliberately narrow. DataHub MCP supplies identity,
schema, and bounded lineage. EvidenceBound applies the Restricted AST
Policy and Fail-Closed Bounded Interpreter, then emits the Proof Pack
and Native Description Receipt. The final decision is Mandatory Human
Review.
